BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Civic Meetup #561: Dark patterns 2.0: Manipulative design in the a
 ge of AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260922T210000
UID:53446ca98e5fe6f562701332a7afcc7f@guild.host
DESCRIPTION:New technologies and organizations’ practices are regularly 
 placing pressures and challenges on our privacy and transparency rights. T
 his month\, Civic Tech Toronto and the Information and Privacy Commissione
 r of Ontario are highlighting the work to defend\, enforce\, explain and u
 pdate these rights. To see all September events\, check our events listing
  on Guild.&#x20\;\n\n‎‎\n\nTopic: Dark patterns 2.0: Manipulative desi
 gn in the age of AI\n\n"Dark patterns" are user interface design tactics t
 hat influence users to make choices that benefit an online service. Tradit
 ionally\, dark patterns have relied on visual design elements and encourag
 ed superficial user actions like clicking a button. However\, dark pattern
 s are now appearing in interactive dialogue between users and AI chatbots.
  This talk discusses why AI dark patterns may pose novel privacy risks and
  be especially difficult to resist – especially for young users.\n\n‎
 ‎\n\nSpeaker: Dominique Kelly \\[joining remotely]\n\nDominique Kelly is
  a Postdoctoral Associate in the Faculty of Information and Media Studies 
 at Western University. Her research interests include dark patterns\, data
  privacy\, and the social and cognitive effects of interacting with genera
 tive AI.\n\n‎\n\nAgenda:\n\n7:00-7:20 Welcome and Introductions\n\n7:20-
 7:50 Presentation and Q\\&A/discussion\n\n7:50-9:00 Breakout groups\n\n‎
